Description: Software Sources configuration tool for Debian
 Configure the sources for installable software and updates on Debian
 and Debian Menta:
  * choose an official Debian mirror, the archive components (main,
    contrib, non-free, non-free-firmware) and the update suites
    (security, updates, backports, proposed-updates)
  * enable source code and debug symbol repositories
  * manage third party repositories and their authentication keys
  * fix common APT problems and find foreign packages
 .
 The official repositories are kept in deb822 format in
 /etc/apt/sources.list.d/debian.sources. Mirrors come from the Debian
 mirror masterlist, the same list the Debian installer offers.
 .
 The interface runs as the desktop user, on X11 and Wayland. Changes
 to the system go through a small helper started with pkexec.
